\section{Results}
The original result chart uses the laboratory palette and exact values are reported below.
\begin{figure}[!ht]
\centering
\begin{tikzpicture}
\begin{axis}[
    width=9cm,
    height=6cm,
    xlabel={Metric},
    ylabel={Score},
    ymin=0.65, ymax=0.95,
    symbolic x coords={Accuracy,Recall},
    xtick=data,
    ymajorgrids=true,
    grid style={gray!20},
    nodes near coords,
    legend pos=north west,
]
\addplot[labblue, mark=*, thick] coordinates {(Accuracy,0.81) (Recall,0.74)};
\addlegendentry{Base}
\addplot[laborange, mark=square*, thick] coordinates {(Accuracy,0.86) (Recall,0.79)};
\addlegendentry{New}
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
\caption{Performance trend}
\label{fig:performance}
\end{figure}
The exact values are Base: 0.81 and 0.74; New: 0.86 and 0.79.
